<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sugar Ray Robinson returns two weeks after intake with his care partner and is seen the same day by Dr. Haddad-Kowalski at the memory clinic. He had a brain MRI and a hearing test this morning. His intake blood count, kidney function, B12 and TSH were normal; hemoglobin A1c was 6.4%. He has slept well since stopping the over-the-counter sleep aid. He has not driven since intake; his care partner drives. The handgun stays unloaded and locked with the key held by his care partner. He repeated one question twice during the visit and laughed about it. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>MMSE</td><td>22</td></tr><tr><td>CDR</td><td>Global 1, sum of boxes 5.5</td></tr><tr><td>MRI</td><td>Hippocampal atrophy; six microbleeds; no superficial siderosis; cavum septi pellucidi</td></tr><tr><td>Audiometry</td><td>Mild to moderate bilateral high-frequency hearing loss</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Sleeping well without diphenhydramine</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
